8a7b9ef7183e"}},{"id":"baebf32719f55a3f5864922f4d77a4bd6dfb69307507c15a654ede3fda416204","quote":"We are a commercial-stage biopharmaceutical company focused on developing and commercializing therapies for people with chronic endocrine and neurological diseases in the United States. We offer Recorlev for the treatment of endogenous hypercortisolemia in patients with Cushing’s syndrome, Gvoke for the treatment of severe hypoglycemia, and Keveyis for the treatment of Primary Periodic Paralysis (\"PPP\"). We are advancing our Phase 3-ready pipeline product, XP-8121, once-weekly subcutaneous (\"SC\") levothyroxine, which leverages our proprietary technology XeriSol.","context":"Xeris Biopharma Holdings, Inc. along with its subsidiaries, is referenced herein as the \"Company,\" \"Xeris,\" \"Xeris Biopharma,\" \"we\" or \"our.\" Throughout this document, unless otherwise noted, references to Gvoke include Gvoke PFS, Gvoke HypoPen, and Gvoke Kit.","section":"ITEM 2. MANAGEMENT’S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS","block":280,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001867096-26-000065","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-06","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001867096","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1867096/000186709626000065/xers-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/06b3ac64eeaff0bdcd50cee67841906a206966075c4cc63766848a7b9ef7183e.bin","sha256":"06b3ac64eeaff0bdcd50cee67841906a206966075c4cc63766848a7b9ef7183e"}},{"id":"9e84958a78cd32388e2bc062001ffea35520cfc427efed7d57e65bc2883db499","quote":"Our top priority is maximizing the potential of our three commercial products:","context":"Commercial Products","section":"ITEM 2. MANAGEMENT’S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS","block":282,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001867096-26-000065","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-06","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001867096","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1867096/000186709626000065/xers-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/06b3ac64eeaff0bdcd50cee67841906a206966075c4cc63766848a7b9ef7183e.bin","sha256":"06b3ac64eeaff0bdcd50cee67841906a206966075c4cc63766848a7b9ef7183e"}},{"id":"c9f25d9c7b7f44ffdb8c6d476eba55bfcd7675f731ac7e30081738242e2403ff","quote":"•Recorlev is a cortisol synthesis inhibitor approved for the treatment of endogenous hypercortisolemia in adult patients with Cushing's syndrome for whom surgery is not an option or has not been curative. Endogenous Cushing's syndrome is a rare but serious and potentially fatal endocrine disease caused by chronic elevated cortisol exposure.","context":"Our top priority is maximizing the potential of our three commercial products:","section":"ITEM 2. MANAGEMENT’S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS","block":283,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001867096-26-000065","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-06","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001867096","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1867096/000186709626000065/xers-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/06b3ac64eeaff0bdcd50cee67841906a206966075c4cc63766848a7b9ef7183e.bin","sha256":"06b3ac64eeaff0bdcd50cee67841906a206966075c4cc63766848a7b9ef7183e"}},{"id":"3343155354dfc7fa472d549a2580f457bcff3d6db9dd597713e6d61310ee7dbe","quote":"•Gvoke is a ready-to-use, liquid-stable glucagon for the treatment of severe hypoglycemia. The product is indicated for use in pediatric and adult patients with diabetes age two years and above and can be administered in two simple steps.","context":"•Recorlev is a cortisol synthesis inhibitor approved for the treatment of endogenous hypercortisolemia in adult patients with Cushing's syndrome for whom surgery is not an option or has not been curative. Endogenous Cushing's syndrome is a rare but serious and potentially fatal endocrine disease caused by chronic elevated cortisol exposure.","section":"ITEM 2. MANAGEMENT’S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS","block":284,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001867096-26-000065","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-06","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001867096","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1867096/000186709626000065/xers-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/06b3ac64eeaff0bdcd50cee67841906a206966075c4cc63766848a7b9ef7183e.bin","sha256":"06b3ac64eeaff0bdcd50cee67841906a206966075c4cc63766848a7b9ef7183e"}},{"id":"38a1294a156fc1499afd9e7fc545d8948b04b3946922746e4b870b3905d53d6c","quote":"•Keveyis is the first therapy approved in the United States to treat hyperkalemic, hypokalemic, and related variants of PPP. PPP is a rare genetic, neuromuscular disorder that can cause extreme muscle weakness and/or paralysis; some forms are also commonly associated with myotonia or muscle stiffness.","context":"•Gvoke is a ready-to-use, liquid-stable glucagon for the treatment of severe hypoglycemia. The product is indicated for use in pediatric and adult patients with diabetes age two years and above and can be administered in two simple steps.","section":"ITEM 2. MANAGEMENT’S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS","block":285,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001867096-26-000065","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-06","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001867096","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1867096/000186709626000065/xers-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/06b3ac64eeaff0bdcd50cee67841906a206966075c4cc63766848a7b9ef7183e.bin","sha256":"06b3ac64eeaff0bdcd50cee67841906a206966075c4cc63766848a7b9ef7183e"}},{"id":"2f65a77b31128f4330faaf91ebabbf1f52dfbf43a592246daa6f0778f4d81b88","quote":"Our company name, Xeris, is derived from the ancient Greek word xērós meaning 'dry' or 'without water/non-aqueous'. Our proprietary, non-aqueous formulation capabilities are designed to enable the convenient injection of medicines previously uninjectable or poorly injectable when utilizing aqueous approaches. Both XeriSol and XeriJect offer the opportunity to create ready-to-use, room-temperature stable, highly concentrated, injectable formulations of both small and large molecules.","context":"Our Pipeline","section":"ITEM 2. MANAGEMENT’S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS","block":287,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001867096-26-000065","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-06","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001867096","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1867096/000186709626000065/xers-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/06b3ac64eeaff0bdcd50cee67841906a206966075c4cc63766848a7b9ef7183e.bin","sha256":"06b3ac64eeaff0bdcd50cee67841906a206966075c4cc63766848a7b9ef7183e"}},{"id":"99ce1900aa6701977f37e4d0ced5bb9cad4744cb4a80c8d29ed8ae997c5706f4","quote":"•XP-8121: We are in the process of developing the first and only, once-weekly, subcutaneous injection of levothyroxine for the treatment of hypothyroidism. We are working with the United States Food and Drug Administration (\"FDA\") and plan to initiate a Phase 3 clinical trial of our XP-8121 product candidate.","context":"Our company name, Xeris, is derived from the ancient Greek word xērós meaning 'dry' or 'without water/non-aqueous'. Our proprietary, non-aqueous formulation capabilities are designed to enable the convenient injection of medicines previously uninjectable or poorly injectable when utilizing aqueous approaches. Both XeriSol and XeriJect offer the opportunity to create ready-to-use, room-temperature stable, highly concentrated, injectable formulations of both small and large molecules.","section":"ITEM 2. MANAGEMENT’S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS","block":288,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001867096-26-000065","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-06","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001867096","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1867096/000186709626000065/xers-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/06b3ac64eeaff0bdcd50cee67841906a206966075c4cc63766848a7b9ef7183e.bin","sha256":"06b3ac64eeaff0bdcd50cee67841906a206966075c4cc63766848a7b9ef7183e"}},{"id":"c7159778d4a85673c719df4e2523bbe2d4435cc072c7d5af412e2f366678e098","quote":"•Partnerships: We are pursuing formulation and development partnerships to apply our XeriSol and XeriJect formulation technologies to enhance the drug delivery and clinical profile of other companies’ proprietary drugs and biologics. We are","context":"•XP-8121: We are in the process of developing the first and only, once-weekly, subcutaneous injection of levothyroxine for the treatment of hypothyroidism. We are working with the United States Food and Drug Administration (\"FDA\") and plan to initiate a Phase 3 clinical trial of our XP-8121 product candidate.","section":"ITEM 2. MANAGEMENT’S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS","block":289,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001867096-26-000065","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-06","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001867096","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1867096/000186709626000065/xers-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/06b3ac64eeaff0bdcd50cee67841906a206966075c4cc63766848a7b9ef7183e.bin","sha256":"06b3ac64eeaff0bdcd50cee67841906a206966075c4cc63766848a7b9ef7183e"}},{"id":"009d6e5627fa7156c492c5d1